  "Immutable. The window runs to completion; time-up opens launch regardless of how much was raised.",
  "Duration",
  "[aria-label] Genesis window",
  "3 hours",
  "24 hours",
  "72 hours",
  "/// PACT",
  "Immutable rules",
  "Genesis supply",
  "8.4M",
  "·",
  "40%",
  "Ladder supply",
  "12.6M",
  "·",
  "60%",
  "Ladder shelves",
  "4,000 · 2000× span",
  "Opening price",
  "1.10× genesis",
  "Deadline to open the pool",
  "7 days",
  "Fixed at deploy, and unsold supply is never re-mintable. Genesis splits 55% to depositor claims and the rest to pool liquidity, which is what opens the market above what they paid. The clock starts when genesis closes: the owner opens the pool inside it, or every depositor can take back 100% of their TQUOTE — with no deadline of their own to beat. A raise that finishes too small to open a pool skips the clock entirely and refunds the moment genesis closes.",
